<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 April, from 1349 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mazandaran.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1349">1349 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">677 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The murder of Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan ends the Bavand dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiya-afrasiyab">Kiya Afrasiyab</a> murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-dawla-hasan">Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan</a>, last ruler of the Bavand dynasty, in a bath, during a revolt of the nobles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrasiab">Afrasiyab</a> took over the Bavandid lands, ending a dynasty that had ruled since 651.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-dawla-hasan">Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1362">1362 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">664 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Teutonic Order captures and destroys Kaunas Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a month-long siege, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> captured and destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaunas">Kaunas</a> Castle, the first brick castle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. Its commander Vaidotas, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kestutis">Kęstutis</a>, and 36 others were taken captive.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-crusade">Lithuanian Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus and the Spanish Crown agree the Capitulations of Santa Fe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ferdinand and Isabella agreed terms with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> for a westward voyage, promising him the title of admiral and a tenth of the wealth from any lands he found.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luther is summoned to recant before the Diet of Worms</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> acknowledged his books but asked for time to answer whether he would retract them. The next day he refused, defying both emperor and Pope.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1895">1895 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">131 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Shimonoseki ends the First Sino-Japanese War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> recognised Korean independence, ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Pescadores</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and paid a large indemnity. Defeat exposed the weakness of the Qing and announced Japan as a regional power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Last French troops leave Syria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The withdrawal of the final French forces completed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>'s independence after a quarter-century of mandate rule. The day is still marked in Syria as Evacuation Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cuban exiles land at the Bay of Pigs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A CIA-trained brigade of some 1,400 Cuban exiles landed in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. They were defeated within three days, a grave embarrassment for the new Kennedy administration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Khmer Rouge take Phnom Penh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> forces entered the Cambodian capital and immediately drove its population into the countryside. Their rule until 1979 led to the deaths of an estimated 1.5 to 2 million people.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 17 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-de-valdivia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro de Valdivia</span><span class="tp">1497–1553</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-elector-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilian-i-elector-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilian I, Elector of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1573–1651</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/taksin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/taksin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Taksin</span><span class="tp">1734–1782</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sirimavo-bandaranaike"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sirimavo-bandaranaike.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sirimavo Bandaranaike</span><span class="tp">1916–2000</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 17 April <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-of-molesme"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-of-molesme.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert of Molesme</span><span class="tp">c. 1028–1111</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marino-faliero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marino-faliero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marino Faliero</span><span class="tp">c. 1285–1355</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kateri-tekakwitha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kateri-tekakwitha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kateri Tekakwitha</span><span class="tp">1656–1680</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sor-juana-ines-de-la-cruz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sor-juana-ines-de-la-cruz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sor Juana Inés de la Cruz</span><span class="tp">c. 1648–1695</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-i-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph I, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1678–1711</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benjamin-franklin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benjamin Franklin</span><span class="tp">1706–1790</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-bautista-sacasa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-bautista-sacasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan Bautista Sacasa</span><span class="tp">1874–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alan-garcia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alan-garcia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alan García</span><span class="tp">1949–2019</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
